WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.730
Violent chaos unfolds across the shoreline.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:08.381
Huge fleshy tendrils slither out of the water,
grabbing people who try to flee and dragging

00:00:08.381 --> 00:00:13.780
them into the depths, as giant harpoons made
of bone whizz across the beach, cutting down

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.209
unfortunate sunbathers in droves.

00:00:16.209 --> 00:00:22.350
It’s a terrifying massacre, but you’d
never in a million years be able to guess

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.480
its source…

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:29.240
On April 10, 2010, something strange began
to happen in the Three Portlands.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.270
Now, the anomalous, extradimensional city-state
that overlaps with the locations of Portland,

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:40.841
Oregon, Portland, Maine, and the Isle of Portland
is no stranger to unusual occurrences, so

00:00:40.841 --> 00:00:44.590
it took the population a little while to notice
that something was happening.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:50.360
But, for some unknown reason, sailboats and
motorboats were beginning to vanish from the

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.360
city.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.070
The disappearances occurred overnight, when
there was no one around to witness them, but

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:00.350
slowly the citizens began to notice that their
friends and family members were going out

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.770
in their watercrafts, and never returning
home.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:09.070
By April 15, the civilians were becoming noticeably
concerned, fearing the worst.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:15.750
On April 16, their worst fears were confirmed
when two local ghosts, Onkar Ahmad and Greg

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.930
Moore, went for a nighttime stroll along the
Harbor.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:23.409
They heard a sudden commotion, and rushed
to the scene of the disturbance.

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:28.600
They arrived just in time to see a living
individual being dragged into the watery depths

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.590
by a large, vein-like tendril.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:35.390
Ahmad asked Greg to wait on land, while he
ventured out into the water to look for the

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:36.390
victim.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:40.620
Unfortunately, Ahmad never came back, and
Greg took his story to the Three Portlands

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.200
Police Department.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:47.601
After waiting a few days for the local man-eating
clam population to migrate, the FBI Unusual

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:51.040
Incidents Unit mounted a formal investigation.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.600
On the morning of April 17th, all of the missing
vehicles suddenly reappeared.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.790
This left the UIU, and the people of the city,
with even more questions.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:01.560
Where had the boats all gone?

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.189
Why were they suddenly back?

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:08.009
And what had happened to the missing people,
who had not been returned along with them?

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:13.700
On April 19th, UIU agents dove into the harbor
to search for any unusual activity, and while

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:18.780
they didn't spot anything especially strange,
they did discover that there were fewer animals

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.730
in the harbor than usual.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:25.700
On April 21, the threat that had been preying
on the citizens of Three-Portlands actually

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.209
made itself known.

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:34.140
At 11:19 AM, 17 boats moved away from the
docks on their own, drifting up onto shore

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.320
though no one could be seen captaining any
of them.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:42.460
As the boats lined up, they began to form
a wall blocking access to the water.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:45.459
No one could get in, or out.

00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:50.700
Civilians watched in shock as the boats began
to warp and change before their eyes, growing

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:57.220
thick masses of scales on their surfaces,
sprouting harpoon guns that fired boney projectiles,

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:01.200
and slashing veiny tendrils at anyone within
reach.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.709
The citizens began to panic, running in every
direction in an attempt to escape the monstrous

00:03:06.709 --> 00:03:07.709
boats.

00:03:07.709 --> 00:03:11.840
But they were too slow to evade the attacks,
and the boats snatched them off of the shore

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:16.810
and yanked them aboard, using their harpoons
to impale those who managed to run further

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:18.890
than the tendrils could stretch.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:24.320
As the army of fleshy boats closed in around
the shore, a tugboat broke the surface of

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.320
the water.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:31.310
Unlike the rest of the boats, it had a noticeable
hole in its hull, and was missing its wheelhouse.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:36.770
At an unnaturally quick pace, the tugboat
began to advance onto land, using its tendrils

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:41.900
to drag itself along the shore and into the
more populous part of town.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:47.129
It grabbed civilians at random, absorbing
their blood into its metallic surface as it

00:03:47.129 --> 00:03:48.129
went.

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:52.730
Suddenly, it spotted Albert Izatt, a noted
member of the Church of the Broken God, and

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.670
began to focus its attack on him.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:04:00.610
But before the tugboat monster could reach
Izatt, a city security golem interfered.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:05.879
Sadly, though the golem put up a valiant fight,
the anomaly was able to destroy it by falling

00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:10.959
onto it again and again until the golem was
no longer able to get back up.

00:04:10.959 --> 00:04:16.440
There are few creatures that would survive
having a boat drop itself on top of them repeatedly,

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.269
and sadly the security golem was not one of
them.

00:04:19.269 --> 00:04:24.620
With the golem out of the way, the boat continued
to drag itself through the streets wildly,

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:29.570
crashing through the side of a local restaurant
where its owner, an entity known as THE GRUEL,

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.830
was in the middle of a busy brunch service.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:37.990
At the sight of the invading watercraft, THE
GRUEL set down his pitcher of bottomless mimosas,

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:42.720
wiped his hands on his apron, and grabbed
his trusty dual-wield swords from underneath

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:43.910
the counter.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:48.260
He kept them there in case someone attempted
to dine and dash, but he figured they would

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.470
do just fine against a blood-drinking tugboat.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:56.690
While THE GRUEL kept the tugboat busy, UIU
forces were able to break through the barricade

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:02.350
of boats for a brief period of time, allowing
more security golems to enter the area, as

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:05.040
well as allowing more citizens to escape.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:10.570
Unfortunately, this little victory was short-lived
as further unforeseen horrors drudged themselves

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:11.770
up from the deep.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:16.130
The reanimated corpses of various species
native to the harbor began to crawl out of

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:21.030
the water, surrounding THE GRUEL and allowing
the tugboat to escape the fight.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:25.880
As it made its way back to the harbor, every
boat it passed attempted to toss bodies onto

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:29.090
the tugboat, covering it in fresh blood.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:33.280
Slowly but surely, the damage to the tugboat
began to repair itself.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:38.520
Once the boat had regained its strength, it
set its sights on a previously untouched cargo

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.520
ship.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:43.650
An observing UIU officer determined that the
boat was somehow attempting to convert the

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:48.770
cargo ship, to transform it into another one
of its fleshy allies.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:54.870
But before the transformation could take place,
a cargo crate broke open, spilling over 1,000

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.210
hardtack crackers.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:59.160
Suddenly, the tugboat stopped everything that
it was doing.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:04.380
It took one tendril, and began to count each
individual cracker that had spilled out.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:09.720
While the tugboat was distracted with its
task, a citizen offered the UIU use of their

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:15.370
"rare metals cannonball collection" in the
fight to apprehend the aggressive boat.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:20.250
One particular cannonball, made from electrum,
was able to puncture the hull of one of the

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:23.139
infected ships, rendering it motionless.

00:06:23.139 --> 00:06:26.840
They were elated to have found a weapon that
worked against these boats!

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:30.690
While the tugboat continued to count, the
remaining townspeople gathered all of the

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:35.000
electrum they could find, and began to fight
back against the boats.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:39.650
One by one, the boats sank, and all the while
the tugboat continued to count.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:44.220
In the meantime, UIU officers managed to free
THE GRUEL from his zombie attackers.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:49.190
They presented him with an electrum cannonball,
which he proceeded to punch finger holes into

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:51.110
and wield like a bowling ball.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.690
Then, THE GRUEL had a score to settle.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:59.430
No one, whether human, ghost, or tugboat,
was going to mess with his brunch.

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:04.180
THE GRUEL barreled toward the harbor, grabbed
hold of the still-distracted tugboat, and

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:06.850
punched it hard with his cannonball fist.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:11.810
If the tugboat could breathe, the punch would
have knocked the air out of its lungs.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:16.380
THE GRUEL then threw the tugboat out of the
water and continued the savage beating, before

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.850
preparing to destroy the battered vehicle
once and for all.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:25.620
He lifted it up into the air, jumped up to
follow it, and hit it with so much force that

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:30.720
the tugboat careened through the air, colliding
with a portal that transported it to the Isle

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:31.720
of Portland.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:35.591
Luckily, this particular portal could only
be unlocked via a high-speed impact from a

00:07:35.591 --> 00:07:37.440
water-based vehicle.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:42.050
Speaking of luck, an SCP Foundation team was
returning to the Isle from a failed mission

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:45.870
just as the anomalous boat appeared in their
reality.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:49.990
The object was knocked unconscious by the
impact of its travel (and the beating from

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:55.180
THE GRUEL), and in its incapacitated state,
it was transported to a nearby Foundation

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:56.180
Site.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:08:00.470
There, it was contained and given the designation
of SCP-6426.

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:04.909
Due to its anomalous traits including the
consumption of blood, a talent for hypnosis,

00:08:04.909 --> 00:08:10.930
and a compulsive counting habit, it was also
given the nickname The Vampire Boat.

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:17.210
SCP-6426 is a Keter-class, sapient, hostile
entity that, in an inactive state, bears the

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:21.800
appearance of a harbor tugboat in a constant
state of rust and degradation.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:26.569
Any blood (or organs containing blood) that
comes into contact with the boat will be absorbed

00:08:26.569 --> 00:08:30.960
through the metal, causing the degradation
to visibly improve as a result.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:35.990
The most effective blood appears to come from
humans, cetaceans, and a few specific species

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:37.810
of selachians.

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:42.440
The entity does not only use the absorbed
blood to improve its appearance, but is also

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:47.520
capable of using it to create organic additions
to its body, including the vein-like tendrils

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:53.301
spotted in the Three Portlands, cognitohazardous
eyes attached to bending eyestalks, harpoon

00:08:53.301 --> 00:08:59.370
guns, and cannons capable of firing ammunition
made from anomalous species of barnacles.

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:05.490
These barnacles are capable of reanimating
dead tissue on contact, and SCP-6426 frequently

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:13.261
uses them to create instances of SCP-6426-C,
masses of reanimated tissue that the boat

00:09:13.261 --> 00:09:15.790
uses to aid in its attacks or self-defense.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:23.070
SCP-6426 uses its tendrils to grab prey and
drag them toward itself, but the tendrils

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:25.120
serve an additional purpose as well.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:30.170
Each of the tendrils has a mouth on the tip,
similar in structure to that of the North

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.320
American Medicinal Leech.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:36.610
When the tendril has made contact with its
prey, the mouth will then bite into the spinal

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:41.250
column of the creature, causing its brain
function to cease as its canines grow long

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:47.850
and hollow, hard scales form on their skin,
and their muscle mass and bone density increase.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:53.390
Once they have been transformed in this way,
organisms taken by SCP-6426 are designated

00:09:53.390 --> 00:10:00.839
SCP-6426-A. These instances are used to the
entity's advantage, helping it to extract

00:10:00.839 --> 00:10:06.240
blood from victims at a distance as well as
providing an additional line of defense and

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:07.240
offense.

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:14.570
In the event that SCP-6426 encounters another
watercraft, it is able to use SCP-6426-A to

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:23.510
convert the vehicle into an instance of SCP-6426-B.
These converted boats are similar to SCP-6426,

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.250
and are able to function on their own.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:30.330
However, they are unable to produce their
own eyestalks or cannons, unable to create

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:37.130
SCP-6426-A instances, and do not appear to
be as intelligent as their creator.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:41.180
In the early days of its containment, the
exact nature of the anomaly's intelligence

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:44.149
was the subject of debate amongst the research
staff.

00:10:44.149 --> 00:10:49.660
However, on one specific occasion, the Foundation
was able to establish a line of direct communication

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:57.460
with SCP-6426, and conduct the first (and
so far, the only) interview with the vampiric

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.460
tugboat.

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:02.430
The inciting incident occurred when the arrival
of the Foundation's latest hardtack shipment

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:07.529
was delayed, leaving the boat with nothing
to count and nothing to keep it occupied.

00:11:07.529 --> 00:11:11.940
Freed from the bounds of counting, it managed
to escape and grab hold of several Foundation

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:14.279
staff members with its tendrils.

00:11:14.279 --> 00:11:18.351
After chasing the boat through the site, guards
were able to corner it, prompting the boat

00:11:18.351 --> 00:11:23.510
to absorb the bodies it had taken, and use
the organic material to produce a siren that

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:26.050
emitted the sound of a human voice.

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:32.500
It is through this siren that SCP-6426 responded
to interview questions, using the voice of

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.820
one of its victims.

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:39.330
Junior Researcher Sajad Williamson, in spite
of his protests, was selected to conduct the

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:40.330
interview.

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:44.639
His fellow staff members refused to take no
for an answer, and as the newest hire, the

00:11:44.639 --> 00:11:47.120
unpleasant job fell on his shoulders.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:52.209
Much to everyone's surprise, the anomaly began
the conversation rather politely, saying:

00:11:52.209 --> 00:11:53.450
"I am…

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:54.690
SO sorry.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:58.240
I thought you were those self-righteous lunatics
from the church.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:04.150
I apologize profusely for any trouble I may
have caused, and I want to point out I fully

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:05.430
support your mission.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:09.139
Yes… our first line of defense against the
undersea menace!

00:12:09.139 --> 00:12:11.589
I am more than willing to punch sharks.

00:12:11.589 --> 00:12:12.589
Selachians!

00:12:12.589 --> 00:12:13.589
Yes, right.

00:12:13.589 --> 00:12:16.399
Haha… how rude of me, yes."

00:12:16.399 --> 00:12:22.339
Dr. Williamson's first question concerned
SCP-6426's apparent intended victim back in

00:12:22.339 --> 00:12:24.730
Three-Portlands: Albert Izatt.

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:26.480
SCP-6426 responded:

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:27.480
"Albert?

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:30.070
His first name is really Albert?

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:31.070
Huh.

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:36.720
Well, what other relationship is there to
say besides "the hunter" and "the hunted."

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:43.060
Admiral Izatt is a ruthless man, known for
terrorizing and slaughtering people like me.

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:48.889
He was leading a search party of those barbaric
nautiphiles, intending to gut me like a seal."

00:12:48.889 --> 00:12:51.810
"What do you mean by 'people like you'?"

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:52.930
Dr. Williamson inquired.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:56.070
"Free thinkers, of course!

00:12:56.070 --> 00:13:01.010
People who are unafraid to break from the
mold, to carve their own path in life instead

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:05.610
of following the predetermined route set by
that ignorant 'check valve.'

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:11.339
The church is built upon a foundation of lies;
no one's really a petty officer on this ship,

00:13:11.339 --> 00:13:16.480
we're all just… cabin boys, stumbling around
in the dark as we follow the commands of an

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.149
off-hands C.O.B.

00:13:18.149 --> 00:13:26.200
Heh heheh… if you want real power, real
freedom, all you have to do is listen for

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:27.709
the call of the beast.

00:13:27.709 --> 00:13:33.620
Open the porthole, and he'll squeeze you right
through.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.000
Heheheh…"

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:41.600
Dr. Williamson, feeling rather in over his
head, attempted to convince one of his colleagues

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:42.850
to take over.

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:45.930
When he refused, however, Dr. Williamson continued.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:49.759
"Could you explicate your activities within
the harbor?

00:13:49.759 --> 00:13:52.720
And- and how you arrived there."

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:58.640
"Well, after I got the boatswains off my trail,
I found a cave to hide in- I was forced to

00:13:58.640 --> 00:13:59.640
hide in!

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:00.640
Yes.

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:03.560
Forced to hide deep into the cave, which turned
out to be a tunnel!

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:04.560
Surprising.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:09.440
The tunnel led to some coastal community where
I took refuge; licking my wounds in the safety

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:12.740
of the depths as those zealots stalked the
surface.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:18.560
I spent my time preparing, gathering the strength
necessary to face them once more.

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:22.440
Until I was ambushed, assaulted within my
hideout by a boatswain.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:28.190
I fought for my life as I was forced out into
the open and descended upon by a manner of

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:33.100
monsters and freaks, all of this orchestrated
by that scumbag Izatt.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:36.570
I was beaten within an inch of my life before…

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:37.570
hm.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:41.829
I'm not quite sure what happened after that;
I believe I was knocked unconscious.

00:14:41.829 --> 00:14:45.930
You'll have to illuminate me on how I came
to be in your custody."

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:49.420
At this point, the interview began to veer
in an odd direction.

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:53.660
The boat expressed confusion about the nature
of Williamson's questions, specifically how

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:58.100
little they related to the subject of sharks,
and punching them.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:02.290
It was at this point that the Site Director
sought guidance from the Multi-U Department.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:06.149
A researcher there informed Williamson about
the confusion.

00:15:06.149 --> 00:15:13.750
SCP-6426 had mistaken the SCP Foundation for
another organization, the Shark Punching Center.

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:18.470
Dr. Williamson resumed the interview, prepared
to play along and keep the boat comfortable.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:21.100
Unfortunately, Williamson was a terrible liar.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:24.290
"Yes, we are the Shark Punching Centre.

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:29.570
We will determine if you are a suitable candidate
to carry out the mission: to search, punch,

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:32.589
and contain shar- I mean selachians."

00:15:32.589 --> 00:15:37.330
This verbal misstep caused SCP-6426 to become
suspicious.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:41.120
After a moment, it pieced together the truth
and began to throw itself against the wall

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.790
in a desperate attempt to escape.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:47.519
It was apprehended by security guards, who
impaled it with a naval ram and returned the

00:15:47.519 --> 00:15:49.800
watercraft to its containment cell.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:54.120
The exact reason for its apparent fear and
hatred of the Foundation is currently unknown,

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:57.740
and the boat has made no attempt to speak
since.

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:04.079
Currently, SCP-6426 is kept in a 39m x 39m
x 50m containment chamber.

00:16:04.079 --> 00:16:06.830
Beneath the chamber, there is an artificial
lava tube.

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:11.870
The tugboat has a navel ram through its hull
and engine, holding it in place.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:17.160
This ram is checked daily for signs of degradation,
as it is the primary force keeping the anomaly

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.160
immobile.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:23.050
If the ram is ever removed, or damaged somehow,
a failsafe system will activate, releasing

00:16:23.050 --> 00:16:28.020
100 hardtack crackers and two pieces of electrum
into the containment chamber.

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:32.399
This is intended to keep the tugboat occupied
until the naval rod can be replaced.

00:16:32.399 --> 00:16:38.020
If, for some reason, the naval rod fails and
the boat runs out of hardtack to count...well,

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:42.630
there will be nowhere, on water or land, that
we can hide.

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:49.931
Now go check out “SCP-1861 - The Crew of
the HMS Wintersheimer” and “SCP-4217 - Contain

00:16:49.931 --> 00:16:50.839
The Bismarck.”

